      "username": "BurhanuddinNathdwara",
      "name": "Burhanuddin Murtaza",
      "created_at": "2025-08-29T11:33:42.555Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I am setting up ERPNext on a single server for around 20 companies. We have divided these companies into 3 categories: A, B, and C.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>For Category A companies → Some fields and tabs should be hidden.</li>\n<li>For Category B companies → A different set of fields/tabs should be hidden.</li>\n<li>For Category C companies → Everything should remain visible (no fields hidden).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>To manage this, I have already added a custom field in the Company doctype called “Category of Pakistan”, where I assign the category (A, B, or C) to each company.</p>\n<p>Now my question is:</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/images/emoji/twitter/point_right.png?v=12\" title=\":point_right:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":point_right:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> What is the best way to implement conditional field/tab visibility based on the logged-in user’s company category?</p>\n<p>For example:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Should I fetch the value of <code>category_of_pakistan</code> from the Company doctype and check it inside a Client Script / Server Script to hide or unhide fields?</li>\n<li>Or is there a better/standard way to handle this scenario in ERPNext?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If anyone has an example script snippet for this, it would be really helpful.</p>\n<p>Thanks in advance!</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/ee59a6/{size}.png",
